  "description": "#6548 — an advanced query leaves template pages and the placeholder blocks under them out of its result, as the agenda does, unless the filter names the `template` property. S3 is a template page (its `template` property is set by the one op) holding the placeholder S4; S1/S2 are an ordinary page and block. The empty filter must return S2 and S1 only, so a stack that lists placeholders reds. Naming `template` in a `has-property` leaf returns the template page itself, and naming it inside `has-parent-matching` returns its placeholder, so a stack that drops the exclusion unconditionally (hiding templates from a query that asks for them) reds too.",
